/**
 * Independently re-verified table of the closed-form results already
 * PROVEN in "The Geometry of Disagreement" (Theorems 4.2, 4.8(c), 5.7(a)).
 * Generated by constructing each theorem's own explicit witness vector in
 * code (Python, exact `fractions.Fraction` arithmetic — see the write-up this
 * table was generated alongside), confirming it is genuinely in the dual
 * lattice F*(G) (divergence-free, integer circulation on every fundamental
 * cycle), and checking its max-norm against the closed form exactly. Where
 * the lattice's rank was small enough, `exhaustiveVerified` also means an
 * exhaustive search over that rank-dimensional integer lattice confirmed no
 * shorter nonzero vector exists — i.e. the construction really is μ(G), not
 * merely an upper bound. Do not hand-edit — regenerate from the verification
 * script if the paper's constructions change.
 */

